From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:00:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/57] MAS local: keep crash reports on disk when uploads are
 not enabled

Not for upstream: it is the opposite of the upstream privacy design.

On every boot uploadEntries() asks the consent provider about each report
that was not uploaded. Without -metrics-collection the headless and the
launcher providers answer REMOVE, so the minidump of the previous crash is
deleted before anyone can look at it, and the windowed provider may pop up
a dialog.

When uploads are not enabled, skip the consent query altogether: do not
show a dialog, do not upload, and keep the newest 5 reports (override with
ANDROID_EMU_CRASH_REPORTS_TO_KEEP, 1..100) in the local database, logging
the minidump path of each. Older ones are removed. With uploads enabled the
upstream flow is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:Claude-Opus-5.5
Change-Id: Icbbae812225ad8ce12cdd61ff65f958df64e875c
---
 .../android/crashreport/CrashSytemInit.cpp    | 65 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 65 insertions(+)

